===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|stay}}, from {{der|en|fro|estaye}}, {{m|fro|estaie||a prop, a stay}}, from {{der|en|dum|staeye||a prop, stay}}, a contracted form of {{m|dum|staede}}, {{m|dum|stade}} {{gloss|"a prop, stay, help, aid"; compare {{cog|dum|staeyen}}, {{m|dum|staeden||to make firm, stay, support, hold still, stabilise}}}}, from {{der|en|odt|*stad||a site, place, location, standing}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*stadiz||a standing, place}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-||to stand}}. See above.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[prop]]; a [[support]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=9|passage=My onely strength and '''stay'''.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Italy
|passage=The trees themselves serve, at the same time, as so many '''stays''' for their Vines}}
#* '''April 27, 1823''', {{w|Samuel Taylor Coleridge}}, ''Table Talk''
#*: Lord Liverpool is the single '''stay''' of this ministry.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1831|author=Peter Leicester|title=Arthur of Britanny|page=18|passage=Even when the deceptive mask was torn away, and the broken-hearted parent, beholding the accursed fact, that his darling son, the fancied '''stay''' of his declining age, was enlisted against him in his brother's horrible revolt, cursed them both and died, not even then did one compunctuous visiting touch his callous heart.}}
# A piece of stiff material, such as [[plastic]] or [[whalebone]], used to stiffen a piece of clothing.
#: {{ux|en|Where are the '''stays''' for my collar?}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} A [[corset]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1859|author=w:Wilkie Collins|title=The Woman in White|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/files/583/583-h/583-h.htm
|passage=Her figure was tall, yet not too tall; comely and well-developed, yet not fat; her head set on her shoulders with an easy, pliant firmness; her waist, perfection in the eyes of a man, for it occupied its natural place, it filled out its natural circle, it was visibly and delightfully undeformed by '''stays'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Prior Alma|passage=When Jenny's '''stays''' are newly laced.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[fastening]] for a garment; a [[hook]]; a [[clasp]]; anything to hang another thing on.

